<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the macOS build. Not wired into tauri.macos.conf.json
  yet, on purpose: the team identifier below is a placeholder, and a config
  pointing at a file with a fake identifier would fail the first signed
  build with a confusing error. Add

      "entitlements": "entitlements.plist"

  to the macOS bundle config in the same commit that fills in the real
  identifier, which arrives with the Developer ID certificate.

  Why this exists at all: the Touch ID key lives in the data protection
  keychain (Location::DataProtectionKeychain in the core's enclave backend),
  and that keychain refuses an app which is not signed AND carries no
  keychain access group. Without it, enrolment fails with
  errSecMissingEntitlement even though the signature itself is valid, which
  reads like broken code rather than missing configuration.

  Deliberately nothing else in here. The app needs no JIT, loads no unsigned
  plugins, bundles no external binaries, and touches no camera, microphone
  or location. Every entitlement is an attack surface and a thing to
  justify, so the list stays at what breaks without it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
  <array>
    <string>TEAM_ID_GOES_HERE.com.silentsilo.desktop</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
